  <datafield tag="563" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Side staped in printed paper wrapper. First and last image on vellum paper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Ossabaw was printed by Michael Goodman on a Hamada Star 700 CD Press. The palladium prints were reproduced using a 175-line screen cancelling negative process. The paper is Mohawk Superfine 100 lb. text The type, Paladium, was set by Annette Allyn Day ... The Cover was hand printed using photo silk-screen by William Prankard"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Artist's statement: "By chance I had seen an exhibit of photographs made on the coastal island of Ossabaw by Helen Hamada. The pictures stayed in my mind, and a year later, in the summer of 1979, I went to Ossabaw to photograph ... by coincidence, a woman I knew in Atlanta named Dancing Water, whose given name was Carol Williams, came to the island during my stay. An innovative and unusual dancer, she entered a collaboration with me to create pictures which we thought could become a small book"--Page 3.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition of 300, signed by the artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
